IMPORT prelude

-- Civil Defence Act 1986 (Singapore) -- what the Act asks of, and gives to, people outside the Force: day-to-day operational
-- powers and who may use them (ss 101A, 101B), personal protection from liability (ss 101C, 105, 112), the state of civil
-- defence emergency and its special powers (ss 102, 103), the public warning system on private premises (ss 103A to 103D),
-- obstruction (s 106), SCDF uniforms and insignia (s 106A), officers of a body corporate (s 107), employment protection (s 108)
-- and compensation for injury (s 111).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CDA1986.txt, with
-- amendments to Act 16 of 2026 (in force 30 September 2026) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 11 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the provisions an ordinary
-- person, building owner, business or employer meets. Not encoded: constitution and organisation of the Force (Parts 2, 3),
-- jurisdiction, service offences, arrest, trial and punishment of members (Parts 4 to 8), pay deductions (Part 9), boards of
-- inquiry (Part 10), the Fund (Part 11), training arrangements (s 104), service outside Singapore (Part 13A), General and
-- Standing Orders (s 110), mobilisation (s 113) and regulations (s 115). The prescribed height below which a residential
-- building is not "relevant premises" (s 103A) is set by regulations, which were not retrieved; it is a parameter here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Civil Defence Act 1986 -- the public`

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    `the Commissioner`
    `a member authorised by the Commissioner`
    `a member not so authorised`
    `an ambulance contractor's employee`
    `an SAF serviceman attached to the Force`
    `a police officer`

§§ `101A, 101B -- day-to-day operations`

-- s 101A(1): "The Commissioner or any member authorised by the Commissioner may, if the action authorised by this section
-- appears to him or her to be necessary for the discharge of the function in section 4(1)(c)" [day-to-day operations for the
-- protection of life, health or safety] -- (a) enter and break into any place; (b) remove an impeding vehicle or thing; (c)
-- remove an endangered individual; (d) close any road or way; (e) shut off gas, fuel oil, water or electricity; (f) require a
-- person suspected of exposure in a hazardous materials incident to undergo medical examination and treatment; (g) seize and
-- dispose of contaminated things. (2): take the fingerprints or other personal identifiers of an unknown individual who is
-- "unconscious or otherwise unable to communicate", to facilitate urgent medical care.
-- s 101B(1): the powers in "section 101A(1)(a) to (e) and (2)" may also be exercised by an employee of an emergency ambulance
-- service provider under contract with the Government, and an SAF serviceman attached to the Force for ambulance services.
-- So neither may require a medical examination (f) or seize contaminated things (g).
-- INFERENCE: the necessity condition of s 101A(1) is read as carried over to s 101B persons; and a police officer, not being
-- named, has no power under s 101A (the police may have powers under other Acts, which are not encoded).
DECLARE DayToDayPower IS ONE OF
    `entering or breaking into premises`
    `removing an impeding vehicle or thing`
    `removing an endangered individual`
    `closing a road`
    `cutting off gas, water or electricity`
    `requiring a medical examination after hazmat exposure`
    `seizing contaminated things`
    `taking an unidentified unconscious person's fingerprints`

GIVEN `the power` IS A DayToDayPower
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the power is shared with s 101B persons` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `requiring a medical examination after hazmat exposure` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `seizing contaminated things` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor, `the power` IS A DayToDayPower, `it appears necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the actor may exercise the day-to-day power` IF
    `it appears necessary` AND
        CONSIDER `the actor`
        WHEN `the Commissioner` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a member authorised by the Commissioner` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an ambulance contractor's employee` THEN `the power is shared with s 101B persons` `the power`
        WHEN `an SAF serviceman attached to the Force` THEN `the power is shared with s 101B persons` `the power`
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `101C, 105, 112 -- protection from liability`

-- s 101C: "No liability shall lie personally against the Commissioner or any member, or any person mentioned in section 101B
-- who, acting in good faith AND WITH REASONABLE CARE, does or omits to do anything in the execution or purported execution of
-- this Act."
GIVEN `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a member is personally protected under s 101C` IF
    `acted in good faith` AND `acted with reasonable care`

-- s 105(2): "No act or default done or made by the civil defence volunteer in good faith whilst participating in any civil
-- defence measures or whilst receiving instruction in civil defence shall subject him or her to any personal liability."
-- (3): a volunteer is a person who has agreed to take part in civil defence measures or receives instruction "organised
-- under the authority of the Commissioner". (1): such a volunteer acting in good faith under an order of a member is deemed
-- the Government's agent for the Government Proceedings Act 1956. Good faith alone; no reasonable-care condition.
GIVEN `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `participating in civil defence measures or instruction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a volunteer is personally protected under s 105` IF
    `acted in good faith` AND `participating in civil defence measures or instruction`

-- s 112: "No action or proceeding shall lie or be brought against the Government, any officer or employee of the Government, a
-- member of the Force or any other person acting under any direction given ... under this Act in respect of anything done or
-- omitted to be done in good faith under and for the purposes of this Act during a state of civil defence emergency or a
-- state of emergency." This bars action against the Government itself, not only personal liability.
GIVEN `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `a state of emergency` IS A BOOLEAN, `a state of civil defence emergency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no action lies under s 112` IF
    `acted in good faith` AND (`a state of emergency` OR `a state of civil defence emergency`)

§§ `102 -- state of civil defence emergency`

-- s 102(1): the Minister may declare a state of civil defence emergency in any part or district if it appears that a civil
-- defence emergency "has occurred or may occur". (2) public notice immediately; Gazette as soon as possible. (3): it
-- "terminates on the expiry of the seventh day from the time the state of civil defence emergency is in force". (4): the
-- Minister may, "with the approval of the President", extend it for further periods.
-- INFERENCE: time is counted in days elapsed since the declaration took effect; the state is in force while fewer than 7 days
-- have elapsed, or, if extended with the President's approval, until the end of the extended period (days from the start).
GIVEN `days elapsed` IS A NUMBER, `extended with the President's approval` IS A BOOLEAN, `extended to day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the state of civil defence emergency is in force` IF
        `days elapsed` LESS THAN 7
    OR  (`extended with the President's approval` AND `days elapsed` LESS THAN `extended to day`)

§§ `103 -- special powers during an emergency`

-- s 103(1): "During a state of emergency or a state of civil defence emergency, the Commissioner, a member or a police officer
-- may, if the action ... appears ... necessary" -- (a) direct any person to assist the Force to save life in immediate danger;
-- (b) direct evacuation and exclusion, and remove non-compliers; (c) remove impeding things, breaking into vehicles; (d) enter
-- and break into premises to save life; (e) restrict movement and close roads and public places.
-- Unlike s 101A, ANY member may act (no authorisation needed), and so may a police officer; s 101B persons are not named.
DECLARE EmergencyPower IS ONE OF
    `directing a person to help save life`
    `directing evacuation or exclusion`
    `removing an impeding thing`
    `entering or breaking into premises to save life`
    `closing roads or public places`

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor, `a state of emergency` IS A BOOLEAN, `a state of civil defence emergency` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it appears necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the actor may exercise the emergency powers` IF
    (`a state of emergency` OR `a state of civil defence emergency`) AND `it appears necessary` AND
        CONSIDER `the actor`
        WHEN `an ambulance contractor's employee` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `an SAF serviceman attached to the Force` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 103(2): a person who renders assistance under (1)(a) "is entitled to fair and reasonable remuneration".
-- s 103(3): a person who suffers loss of or damage to property "by reason of the exercise of the powers conferred by
-- subsection (1)(c) and (d)" is entitled to fair and reasonable compensation. Both claimed under regulations (not retrieved).
-- Loss from an evacuation (b) or a road closure (e) is not mentioned.
GIVEN `the power` IS AN EmergencyPower
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `property loss from the power is compensated` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `removing an impeding thing` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `entering or breaking into premises to save life` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the power` IS AN EmergencyPower
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person directed is entitled to remuneration` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `directing a person to help save life` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `103A -- relevant premises`

-- s 103A(1): "relevant premises" means any building or part of a building but does not include "(a) a residential building
-- not exceeding such height as may be prescribed; and (b) any other type of building that may be prescribed". (2): height is
-- measured from the lowest point at ground level to the highest point "(including any structure fixed to the building)".
-- The prescribed height is in regulations not retrieved; it is a parameter.
GIVEN `is residential` IS A BOOLEAN, `height in metres` IS A NUMBER, `prescribed height in metres` IS A NUMBER,
      `is a prescribed excluded type` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the building is relevant premises` IF
        (NOT (`is residential` AND `height in metres` AT MOST `prescribed height in metres`))
    AND (NOT `is a prescribed excluded type`)

§§ `103B -- space for a public warning device`

-- s 103B(1): the Commissioner may direct the owner of relevant premises to provide "at the owner's expense" space or facility
-- and access to install a prescribed civil defence emergency device. (2) a direction may be given "even though the direction
-- may prejudice the contractual obligations of the owner or occupier". (3): "No liability shall lie against any party to a
-- contract ... for ... any breach of the contract where the breach is SOLELY attributable to ... the compliance by that party
-- with any direction". (6): an owner who contravenes a direction -- fine up to $10,000 or 3 years or both, and for a
-- continuing offence a further fine up to $1,000 "for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after
-- conviction".
GIVEN `the breach is solely attributable to compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner is liable for the contract breach` IF
    NOT `the breach is solely attributable to compliance`

GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for an owner defying a warning-device direction` MEANS
    10000 PLUS 1000 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

§§ `103C -- entry to premises`

-- s 103C(1): the Commissioner may enter (a) relevant premises to assess suitability for a device; (b) premises with a device
-- installed to inspect, repair or maintain it. (2): only after notifying the owner "not less than 5 working days before".
-- "working day" excludes Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays (s 103A). (3): DESPITE (2), where the Commissioner "has reason
-- to believe that a civil defence emergency is likely to occur and urgent repairs ... are needed", and entry has been refused
-- or refusal is apprehended, or consent cannot be obtained after reasonable efforts, entry without notice to carry out urgent
-- repairs. The urgent route is for REPAIRS only; an assessment visit always needs the notice.
DECLARE EntryPurpose IS ONE OF
    `assessing suitability`
    `inspecting or maintaining a device`
    `urgent repairs to a device`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS AN EntryPurpose, `working days of notice` IS A NUMBER, `emergency likely` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `refused or refusal apprehended` IS A BOOLEAN, `consent unobtainable after reasonable efforts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entry is authorised` IF
        `working days of notice` AT LEAST 5
    OR  (    `the purpose` EQUALS `urgent repairs to a device`
         AND `emergency likely`
         AND (`refused or refusal apprehended` OR `consent unobtainable after reasonable efforts`))

§§ `103D, 103(4), 106, 106A -- maximum penalties`

-- s 103(4): contravening a direction under s 103 -- $2,000 or 3 months or both.
-- s 103B(6): owner contravening a warning-device direction -- $10,000 or 3 years or both (plus the daily fine).
-- s 103D: "wilfully removes, relocates, destroys, damages or tampers with" a device -- $50,000 or 3 years or both.
-- s 106: "assaults, obstructs, threatens, abuses, insults or intimidates" a person performing duties under the Act -- $5,000
-- or 6 months or both.
-- s 106A(1), (2): misuse of SCDF uniform or insignia -- $2,500 or 6 months or both. (4): making or supplying them -- $10,000 or
-- 3 years or both. (6): offences under (1), (2) and (4) are arrestable.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `defying an emergency direction`
    `owner defying a warning-device direction`
    `tampering with a warning device`
    `obstructing or insulting an officer`
    `misusing SCDF uniform or insignia`
    `a member wearing uniform off duty`
    `making or supplying SCDF uniform or insignia`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `defying an emergency direction` THEN 2000
    WHEN `owner defying a warning-device direction` THEN 10000
    WHEN `tampering with a warning device` THEN 50000
    WHEN `obstructing or insulting an officer` THEN 5000
    WHEN `misusing SCDF uniform or insignia` THEN 2500
    WHEN `a member wearing uniform off duty` THEN 2500
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `defying an emergency direction` THEN 3
    WHEN `owner defying a warning-device direction` THEN 36
    WHEN `tampering with a warning device` THEN 36
    WHEN `obstructing or insulting an officer` THEN 6
    WHEN `misusing SCDF uniform or insignia` THEN 6
    WHEN `a member wearing uniform off duty` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 36

§§ `106A -- SCDF uniforms and insignia`

-- s 106A(1)(a): a person who "is not a member" and "wears or possesses any SCDF uniform, or uses any SCDF insignia" either (i)
-- "for the purpose of personating or representing himself or herself as a member" or (ii) "knowing that it is likely to cause
-- any member of the public to believe that he or she is a member". (3): a defence to (1)(a) or (2) if the accused proves, on a
-- balance of probabilities, (a) the Commissioner's express permission, or (b) use "for the purposes of a public entertainment
-- provided in compliance with the Public Entertainments Act 1958". "use" of insignia includes "driving on a public road a
-- vehicle that has on it any SCDF insignia" (s 106A(7)).
GIVEN `is a member` IS A BOOLEAN, `wears, possesses or uses it` IS A BOOLEAN, `to personate a member` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knowing the public will likely think so` IS A BOOLEAN, `proves the Commissioner's express permission` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proves a licensed public entertainment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the uniform offence` IF
        (NOT `is a member`)
    AND `wears, possesses or uses it`
    AND (`to personate a member` OR `knowing the public will likely think so`)
    AND (NOT `proves the Commissioner's express permission`)
    AND (NOT `proves a licensed public entertainment`)

-- s 106A(1)(d): a non-member who wears or uses SCDF uniform or insignia "in connection with any business, occupation or
-- employment" for the purpose of falsely claiming (i) a fee for services in a matter the Force is dealing with, (ii) that the
-- Force has bought or used the goods or services, or (iii) the Force's sponsorship or approval. The s 106A(3) defences
-- apply only to (1)(a) and (2), so the public-entertainment and permission defences do not reach (1)(d).
GIVEN `is a member` IS A BOOLEAN, `in connection with a business` IS A BOOLEAN, `to falsely claim Force endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proves a licensed public entertainment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the commercial misuse offence` IF
    (NOT `is a member`) AND `in connection with a business` AND `to falsely claim Force endorsement`

-- s 106A(2): "A member who wears an SCDF uniform or uses any SCDF insignia otherwise than (a) in the course of, and for the
-- purpose of, exercising the functions of a member; or (b) for such other purpose authorised in writing by the Commissioner"
-- commits an offence; s 106A(3) defences apply.
GIVEN `exercising a member's functions` IS A BOOLEAN, `authorised in writing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proves the Commissioner's express permission` IS A BOOLEAN, `proves a licensed public entertainment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member commits the off-duty uniform offence` IF
        (NOT `exercising a member's functions`)
    AND (NOT `authorised in writing`)
    AND (NOT `proves the Commissioner's express permission`)
    AND (NOT `proves a licensed public entertainment`)

-- s 106A(4)(b), (c): a person "(whether or not a member)" who sells, gives or provides SCDF uniform or insignia to a person who
-- is neither a member nor permitted under (3). (5): defence if the accused proves (a) reasonable grounds to believe AND did
-- make reasonable inquiries that the recipient was a member or permitted; or (b) received evidence purporting to show it and
-- it was reasonable to, and the accused did, accept it. (4)(a): manufacturing "otherwise than under an agreement with the
-- Government" -- no defence in (5) reaches manufacture, since (5) speaks only of the person to whom it was "sold, given or
-- provided".
GIVEN `recipient is a member or permitted` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonable grounds and reasonable inquiries` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reasonably accepted evidence from the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supplier commits the supply offence` IF
        (NOT `recipient is a member or permitted`)
    AND (NOT `reasonable grounds and reasonable inquiries`)
    AND (NOT `reasonably accepted evidence from the recipient`)

GIVEN `under an agreement with the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the maker commits the manufacture offence` IF
    NOT `under an agreement with the Government`

§§ `107 -- officers of a body corporate`

-- s 107: where a body corporate commits an offence against the Act, its managing director, manager, governing officers,
-- governing-body members and every person taking part in management "are deemed also to have committed the offence ...
-- unless he or she proves that (c) the offence was committed without his or her consent or connivance; AND (d) he or she
-- exercised such diligence to prevent the commission of the offence as he or she ought to have exercised". Both limbs.
GIVEN `the company offended` IS A BOOLEAN, `takes part in management` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proves no consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN, `proves due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is deemed to have committed the offence` IF
        `the company offended`
    AND `takes part in management`
    AND (NOT (`proves no consent or connivance` AND `proves due diligence`))

§§ `108 -- protection of employment rights`

-- s 108: a person who "during a state of emergency or a state of civil defence emergency" is absent from usual employment "by
-- reason of carrying out duties in connection with civil defence measures in any capacity" is not liable for dismissal, loss
-- of vacation leave or other benefits under the applicable industrial award or agreement "by reason only of his or her
-- absence on those duties, whether or not his or her usual employer has consented". Absence outside such a state -- for
-- instance for training -- is not covered by s 108.
GIVEN `a state of emergency` IS A BOOLEAN, `a state of civil defence emergency` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `absent on civil defence duties` IS A BOOLEAN, `the employer consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the absence is protected under s 108` IF
    (`a state of emergency` OR `a state of civil defence emergency`) AND `absent on civil defence duties`

§§ `111 -- compensation for death or injury`

-- s 111: "The Government shall be liable to pay compensation in respect of the loss of life of, or injury to, a person that
-- occurs while that person is (a) engaged in civil defence measures under the authority of the Commissioner; or (b)
-- participating in training for civil defence measures under the control of the Commissioner or a person acting under the
-- authority of the Commissioner", at prescribed rates, out of the Pension Fund. Not limited to a state of emergency.
GIVEN `died or injured` IS A BOOLEAN, `engaged in measures under the Commissioner's authority` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in training under the Commissioner's control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Government must pay compensation` IF
    `died or injured` AND (`engaged in measures under the Commissioner's authority` OR `in training under the Commissioner's control`)
